[V — THE `Field` DROPDOWN IS PHYSICS: 15 pairs x 48 cells, all distinct]
      🔴 fb425. CONTRACT R6 requires BOTH back dropdowns to change PHYSICS.
      `Character` had §G — 48 measured cells. `Field` had a naming assertion, a
      per-option mono tag check and a click test, and NOTHING that measured the six
      options against EACH OTHER. A skeptic deleted two of the six and this cert did
      not move a single line.
      ⚠️ AND THIS GATE DOES NOT USE THE DROPDOWN AS A TOOL. §H and §F's Mix rows use
      `Side Only` as a PROBE (its wet mono-sums to exactly zero by construction), so
      those DO go red if that one option is gutted — but only that one, and only
      because it is load-bearing scaffolding. Nothing below uses a Field for anything
      except as the thing under test.

      THE METRIC. A Field is a 2x2 MATRIX on the finished wet, so the fingerprint has
      to be CHANNEL-ORDERED or `Swap` and `Straight` are identical BY CONSTRUCTION:
      a mono-summed, correlation-only or side/mid metric cannot tell a channel
      exchange from no exchange at all. 30 log bands of L AND 30 of R, level-
      normalised (so this is a magnitude-spectrum distance and law 6 holds), plus
      correlation, side/mid, and the stereo field's own TRAJECTORY (rms + zero-
      crossing rate) because `Orbit` is a rotation in TIME and is magnitude-flat.
      THE BAR IS AN ANCHOR, NOT A NUMBER I CHOSE (fb417): every pair must differ by
      at least a FIFTH of what ONE QUARTER-TURN OF `Width` does through the same
      metric on the same cell — `Width` being the one stereo control nobody argues
      about. The same fifth §F holds `Rate` and `Roam` to.

